+# UC-27 Delete folder design
+
+## Intent and authorized workflow
+
+Implement issue28/FR-FD-05/FR-FD-06: a current owner trashes a visible folder, all currently active descendants and contained active records in one atomic recoverable operation. Retain opaque ciphertext for exactly720hours, restricted association snapshots and operation membership; detach active organization and preserve independently trashed/terminal items. BR07/20/22 and the authorization/lifecycle matrices bind this design. Recipient RO/RW grants allow reading/editing but never owner deletion. Selected owner scope admits the root; the expressly requested cascade includes its active contained subtree even if descendants have no independent profile link.
+
+Architectural addition across Domain/Command/store/HTTP follows the all-open-issues batch: automatic design/plan self-checks, inline TDD, fresh unfiltered six-family coverage, one whole-branch reviewer, exact-head required CI and normal develop integration. Independent formal security/protocol and real-client approval remain development-only deferred; release qualification is mandatory.
+
+## Alternatives and selected architecture
+
+A per-item RecordTrashStore loop creates multiple operations/deadlines and risks partial cascades, so reject it. A one-shot unguarded recursive UPDATE can miss new membership, current expiry and concurrent native edits, so reject it. Use a dedicated FolderTrashStore with current root authority adapted from FolderUpdateStore, a bounded recursive subtree inventory, ordered structural locks, one guarded root write and same-time guarded child/record writes, then one operation/many typed entries/one retention item. No schema/dependency/algorithm changes; introduce a typed FolderAssociationSnapshot matching existing RecordAssociationSnapshot restoration requirements.
+
+## Public boundary
+
+DELETE `/api/folders/{id}` accepts exactly required expectedRevision, a positive safe integer<=9007199254740991. Use canonical lowercase dashed nonzero GUID path, one canonical vault-access header, no query, strict bounded UTF8 JSON/VaultProofBody and no-store. No envelope, edit timestamp, owner/parent/profile/collection/cascade override. Current identity/access required; no new proof challenge, following recoverable record deletion.
+
+200 folder_deleted returns exactly folderId/trashOperationId/revision/serverSequence/deletedAt/purgeAt. Root revision expected+1, safe sequence strictly advances; timestamps UTC microsecond precision with purgeAt-deletedAt exactly30days. Validate store output and trusted context before output; no child inventory, ciphertext, internal IDs, snapshot or key output. Actual shared empty413 and known schema metadata Minors remain before-client-release follow-ups.
+
+Missing identity401 authentication_required; missing handle401 vault_access_required; invalid visible input400 validation_failed; current access/session/selection denial or native-visible nonowner403 vault_access_denied; hidden/absent/trashed/terminal root or ancestor404 not_found. Corrupt relevant native authority or required structural metadata/dependency503 persistence_unavailable; stale/exhausted revisions/sequence, changed inventory or existing typed trash entry409 revision_conflict. Lost-success retry404 preserves first deadline and cannot create/extend an operation. Caller cancellation propagates; internal cancellation/Db/DbUpdate/Timeout/Json/Format and supported wrapped dependencies503.
+
+## Root authority and opaque deletion
+
+Target-first candidate<=1 and complete same-owner active target+self/upward ancestry with null-parent terminus. Current statement-time actor/account/session/selection/generation/policy/expiry and typed terminal checks exactly follow UC26. Own account-wide access or selected actual PF/CF target/ancestor permits owner delete; PR/CR record-only routes cannot permit folder deletion. Native current RO/RW foreign CF routes establish only visible denial, verified every relevant overlapping contributor with one owner/recipient pin parse; no foreign resource locks or content inspection before403. Hidden scope404 precedes stale/corrupt content; relevant active cycle503, unrelated/unselected cycles remain hidden. Never clear selected ProfileId to broaden access.
+
+Owned damaged envelope bytes may be retained unchanged without parsing/decryption, matching record trash. Structural revision/sequence/time/purge consistency still validates for every affected active resource and active external metadata parent. Unrelated content/grants/wrappers do not block owner trash; collection keys, grants and recipient profiles remain unchanged. Recipient views immediately lose all cascade items through existing active-authority predicates, including records directly shared elsewhere.
+
+## Cascade inventory and locking
+
+Take own actor account FOR UPDATE first, then own session FOR UPDATE. Strong own account lock serializes all current same-owner creation/organization/content/move/trash/rotation writers (including those using NO KEY UPDATE), preventing current owner topology phantoms without foreign locks. Determine current visible root and owner permission before inventory. Recursively traverse only active, nonterminal same-owner descendants; stop at independently trashed/terminal branches. Records admitted only when active/nonterminal in an admitted folder. Independently trashed records or folders, their entries, operation IDs, deadlines, ciphertext and memberships remain unchanged. Current detached independent trash does not enter the cascade. A cycle relevant to root authority/inventory fails closed; no infinite recursion or repeated item.
+
+Read all stored direct PF/PR/CF/CR memberships for admitted folders/records, including inactive profile/collection associations; snapshot root/child parent and record folder IDs plus sorted public profile/collection IDs. Collect distinct affected own profiles, collections, selected profile and optional active external root parent. Lock own profiles ordered publicID FOR NO KEY UPDATE; own collections ordered publicID FOR NO KEY UPDATE; union subtree folders plus external parent ordered publicID FOR UPDATE; records ordered publicID FOR UPDATE; each affected typed association row in deterministic key order FOR UPDATE. No grants, foreign account/profile, unrelated folders/records or upward ancestry chains are locked.
+
+Recheck root authority after each potentially waiting lock phase. Reload complete active subtree and stored associations after all locks; reject growth or topology/metadata/membership changes beyond the captured/held inventory with409 rather than using an unheld parent or ignoring a new child. Current same-owner writer serialization plus folder/record UPDATE locks exclude new FK references after target admission. Existing recipient content writers lock collections before folders/records and never lock the foreign owner account/profile; using the same collection-before-content order avoids cycles. Relevant owner creation's leaf-to-root order is serialized by the own account lock before structural locks; real store races must prove this. Future lifecycle/organization writers must preserve this contract, and UC35's separate implicit recipient-account FK audit remains mandatory.
+
+## Atomic writes and retained restore evidence
+
+Validate safe positive revisions/sequences/UTC microsecond editedAt and absent purgeAt for all admitted active folders/records. Max revision on any changed resource/active external parent409; invalid stored counters/time503. Existing typed trash entries for an admitted active resource409, including stale independently restored entries; UC51 must consume/reconcile old entries before re-trash. Use typed resourceKind+GUID matches everywhere; cross-kind aliases cannot hide/conflict unrelated types.
+
+Final guarded root UPDATE embeds full current root authority at statement_timestamp, owner match, expected root revision, original root envelope/sequence/topology and complete captured active subtree/association inventory. This is the operation's authorization linearization; subsequent writes remain in its transaction under held locks. Root sets deletedAt=statement_timestamp, purgeAt=that+720hours, parent=NULL and increments revision/sequence/stamp. Guard miss reloads current error before409. Verify root after write and capture its actual timestamps. Every other captured folder and record is guarded against original revision/sequence/envelope/parent and current active/nonterminal state, uses identical root deletedAt/purgeAt, detaches parent/folder and advances own revision/sequence/stamp once. Unexpected count/state/error rolls back the root and all earlier members.
+
+Remove only direct links targeting admitted folders/records after snapshotting. Bump each distinct active own external profile/collection and surviving immediate root parent once, preserving their envelope/edit time/keys/wrappers/ownership/other memberships. Do not bump trashed subtree folders again or unchanged ancestors/recipient profiles. Guards require original parent revision/sequence and current lifecycle; conflicts/errors roll back every graph change. Validate every changed sequence is safe and greater than its own previous sequence. Sequence gaps on rollback are allowed.
+
+Create exactly one folder-root TrashOperation with the root timestamps, one typed entry per admitted folder/record with original sorted relationship snapshots, and exactly one trash/{operationId} RetentionWorkItem due at purgeAt. Commit once after output/state verification. Snapshot data is server-private and contains only relationship identifiers, no plaintext or usable keys. Existing unavailable retention handler fails closed/retries; this endpoint must not mark physical purge complete. UC51/53 implement association-revalidated cascade restoration and typed physical expiry before release. Retained folders/records remain mandatory in complete protection rotation inventory; rotation may update retained ciphertext but must preserve operation membership/deadlines. Current target sequences are sync foundation; UC48 durable inherited-visibility events remain a release gate.
+
+## Verification
+
+Main: root-only/deep mixed subtree, direct/root/ancestor owned PF and CF scope, actual native Master/PerProfile access, exact six-field output, common720hour deadline, per-member sequence/revision, unchanged ciphertext/edit time/ownership, one operation/many typed entries/one queue, distinct external parent bumps and preserved unrelated/recipient state. Create independent trash using actual RecordTrashStore and an earlier FolderTrashStore call, reload the surviving root revision after parent bumps, then verify the later root operation excludes those detached items and leaves their existing operation/deadline unchanged. Typed-terminal mixed items retain unchanged state; typed aliases do not expand filtering. Actual owner and native recipient GET/list views hide cascaded folders and directly/inherited shared records.
+AF01: strict body/path/header/query/UTF8/forged organization overrides400 before mutation.
+AF02: hidden root/private parent/sibling, record-only scope, removed membership/trash/terminal actor/ancestor; stale and corrupt content404 precedence.
+AF03: invalid identity/handle/current selection/session, real lock-wait expiry at own account/session/profile/collection/folder/record and final root guard; nonowner native RO/RW403 and malformed relevant contributor503; no selection widening.
+AF04: stale root/child/external parent metadata/exhaustion/stale typed entry, one concurrent winner/lost retry404, actual owner creation/record move/association/rotation and recipient folder/record edits, captured inventory growth/decrease409 through existing same-owner folder/record reparenting or existing-parent link insertion before content locks; new entity INSERTs are blocked by the strong account lock/implicit account FK and actual owner creation must wait, winning state unchanged.
+AF05: real Postgres outage, internal versus caller cancellation, active relevant cycle, malformed structural metadata, failure after root/child/record/link/parent/operation/entry/queue stages and regressed/exhausted sequence roll back complete snapshots; clean retry succeeds. Actual complete native protection rotation includes retained cascade entries; omission fails.
+
+EXPLAIN root target1/complete ancestry and recursive subtree excludes unrelated account inventory; captured locks only admitted set+needed external metadata. No production load claim. Fresh Command/Data/native HTTP and final unfiltered six families, actual six-assembly>=90% line coverage and aggregate branch reporting, locked restore/audits/native322x4/helpers36+23/specs/OpenAPI/range whitespace/one review/exact CI.
